From: Alessandro Greco <address-withheld@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] exit: use the real socket error when a connect() fails

When an exit relay's outgoing connect() fails, connection_handle_write_impl()
reads the actual error with getsockopt(SO_ERROR) into `e`, logs it, and then
calls connection_edge_end_errno(), which recomputes the reason from
tor_socket_errno() -- on Unix the macro `(errno)`, which still holds
EINPROGRESS from the non-blocking connect().  EINPROGRESS is not listed in
errno_to_stream_end_reason(), so the default branch is taken and the client
receives END with reason MISC instead of CONNECTREFUSED (or NOROUTE,
TIMEOUT, ...).

The OR branch immediately below already does the right thing, passing `e` to
errno_to_orconn_end_reason().  Do the same for edge connections.

Fixes the case where a client that asks an exit for a closed port is told
"misc" and cannot distinguish a refused connection from an unspecified
failure.

---
 src/core/mainloop/connection.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/core/mainloop/connection.c b/src/core/mainloop/connection.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/src/core/mainloop/connection.c
+++ b/src/core/mainloop/connection.c
@@ -4475,7 +4475,8 @@ connection_handle_write_impl(connection_t *conn, int force)
         log_info(LD_NET,"in-progress connect failed. Removing. (%s)",
                  tor_socket_strerror(e));
         if (CONN_IS_EDGE(conn))
-          connection_edge_end_errno(TO_EDGE_CONN(conn));
+          connection_edge_end(TO_EDGE_CONN(conn),
+                              errno_to_stream_end_reason(e));
         if (conn->type == CONN_TYPE_OR)
           connection_or_notify_error(TO_OR_CONN(conn),
                                      errno_to_orconn_end_reason(e),
